01:05:21.800 --> 01:05:24.200
And we might just tidy up that last back tick

01:05:24.200 --> 01:05:26.120
and bring it all onto one line.

01:05:26.120 --> 01:05:28.360
Let's see this in action, but before we do that,

01:05:28.360 --> 01:05:31.080
I'm just going to log out the response.

01:05:31.080 --> 01:05:34.300
Now I'm going to go for the same vegan fish cream example

01:05:34.300 --> 01:05:36.880
that we've got in the placeholder text.

01:05:36.880 --> 01:05:40.240
And I'll hit generate copy, and let's see what we get.

01:05:40.240 --> 01:05:42.360
And okay, it's working, but look,

01:05:42.360 --> 01:05:44.440
it's given me an ordered list.

01:05:44.440 --> 01:05:47.500
We've got one, two, three, four, five, and six.

01:05:47.500 --> 01:05:49.720
And it looks a little bit longer than 50 words,

01:05:49.720 --> 01:05:51.840
but if we open up the console,

01:05:51.840 --> 01:05:54.160
we can actually see that we've got this,

01:05:54.160 --> 01:05:56.160
and I'll just paste it in here.

01:05:56.160 --> 01:05:58.660
It says finish reason of length.

01:05:58.660 --> 01:06:00.480
And as I'm sure you'll recall,

01:06:00.480 --> 01:06:04.600
that means that OpenAI has actually cut us short.

01:06:04.600 --> 01:06:07.600
And if you look, number six is not complete.

01:06:07.600 --> 01:06:09.680
It just says, grab your vegan dash.

01:06:09.680 --> 01:06:11.800
And at that point we know that OpenAI

01:06:11.800 --> 01:06:13.440
was trying to give us more.

01:06:13.440 --> 01:06:15.860
Now I've tried this several times before recording

01:06:15.860 --> 01:06:17.040
with various prompts,

01:06:17.040 --> 01:06:20.600
and OpenAI really doesn't work that well with word counts.

01:06:20.600 --> 01:06:23.480
The five words or less that we used in a previous challenge

01:06:23.480 --> 01:06:25.020
does seem to work okay,

01:06:25.020 --> 01:06:27.440
but longer word counts often fail.

01:06:27.440 --> 01:06:31.120
Now, interestingly, OpenAI does know how long a tweet is.

01:06:31.120 --> 01:06:34.060
If we were to change this prompt and ask for a tweet,

01:06:34.060 --> 01:06:37.120
it will nearly always deliver something that's tweet length

01:06:37.120 --> 01:06:39.420
and throw in some hashtags as well.

01:06:39.420 --> 01:06:40.920
Okay, let's try something else

01:06:40.920 --> 01:06:43.440
and see if we can make this Advertify app

01:06:43.440 --> 01:06:45.280
work a little bit better.

01:06:45.280 --> 01:06:48.720
We're going to have a look at the few-shot approach.

01:06:48.720 --> 01:06:50.720
The few-shot approach is where we add

01:06:50.720 --> 01:06:53.600
one or more examples to our prompt.

01:06:53.600 --> 01:06:57.760
We do this because it helps the AI understand what we want.

01:06:57.760 --> 01:07:00.500
This is great for more complex tasks.

01:07:00.500 --> 01:07:02.880
So let's refactor our prompt.

01:07:02.880 --> 01:07:05.360
Firstly, I'm going to remove all of the variables

01:07:05.360 --> 01:07:07.600
and actually rewrite this instruction.

01:07:07.600 --> 01:07:10.280
So I've said user product name, a product description,

01:07:10.280 --> 01:07:13.320
and a target market to create advertising copy

01:07:13.320 --> 01:07:14.640
for a product.

01:07:14.640 --> 01:07:16.640
At the moment, we're not doing anything

01:07:16.640 --> 01:07:17.760
with the user input,

01:07:17.760 --> 01:07:20.600
so that's just gonna give us something really, really random.

01:07:20.600 --> 01:07:23.880
But what we're gonna do next is lay out an example.

01:07:23.880 --> 01:07:25.600
So staying inside the backticks,

01:07:25.600 --> 01:07:29.520
I'll come down onto a new line and here's my example.

01:07:29.520 --> 01:07:33.260
So I've got a product name, which is Flask Tie,

01:07:33.260 --> 01:07:34.600
a product description,

01:07:34.600 --> 01:07:36.600
a tie with a pouch to hold liquids

01:07:36.600 --> 01:07:38.360
and a straw to drink through,

01:07:38.360 --> 01:07:42.400
and the product target market is Office Workers.

01:07:42.400 --> 01:07:45.880
Now I've also put some advertising copy right here

01:07:45.880 --> 01:07:49.700
and that advertising copy is about 54 words long,

01:07:49.700 --> 01:07:52.360
which is the kind of length I'm looking for.

01:07:52.360 --> 01:07:53.920
Now, before this is going to work,

01:07:53.920 --> 01:07:55.720
we need to do a couple of things.

01:07:55.720 --> 01:07:58.280
Firstly, we need to bring back our variables

01:07:58.280 --> 01:07:59.540
and we're going to lay them out

01:07:59.540 --> 01:08:02.060
in the same style as our example.

01:08:02.060 --> 01:08:03.920
So in fact, I'm just going to copy and paste

01:08:03.920 --> 01:08:05.440
all of that text.

01:08:05.440 --> 01:08:08.120
And now let's bring in the user inputs.

01:08:08.120 --> 01:08:12.120
So Flask Tie, we can replace with product name.

01:08:12.120 --> 01:08:15.520
Product description, we can replace with product desk.

01:08:15.520 --> 01:08:19.160
And of course, target market will be product target.

01:08:19.160 --> 01:08:23.980
Now advertising copy, we are just going to leave that empty.

01:08:23.980 --> 01:08:25.720
So can you see what we've done here?

01:08:25.720 --> 01:08:27.320
We've given an example

01:08:27.320 --> 01:08:30.560
and then we've given a partly completed example.

01:08:30.560 --> 01:08:34.900
And this space right here is an invitation for OpenAI

01:08:34.900 --> 01:08:36.780
to go and complete.

01:08:36.780 --> 01:08:37.840
And if you'll remember,

01:08:37.840 --> 01:08:40.600
we're using the create completion endpoint.

01:08:40.600 --> 01:08:44.720
So OpenAI is just going to complete this block of text here

01:08:44.720 --> 01:08:47.600
in the same style as this block of text here.

01:08:47.600 --> 01:08:50.020
It's going to recognize that we want it

01:08:50.020 --> 01:08:52.500
to give us something like that,

01:08:52.500 --> 01:08:54.520
but tailored to the three variables

01:08:54.520 --> 01:08:56.340
that we've got right here.

01:08:56.340 --> 01:08:58.980
If we tested this right now, it would likely work.

01:08:58.980 --> 01:09:01.840
But there's one more thing that we can do to help the AI

01:09:01.840 --> 01:09:04.360
and to make our code more readable.

01:09:04.360 --> 01:09:06.360
What we're going to do is separate

01:09:06.360 --> 01:09:08.760
our instructions and context.

01:09:08.760 --> 01:09:11.440
Now OpenAI docs suggest that you can do this

01:09:11.440 --> 01:09:14.400
with three inverted commas or three hash symbols.

01:09:14.400 --> 01:09:16.760
I'm just going to go for the hash symbols.

01:09:16.760 --> 01:09:19.160
And I'm going to put one set right here

01:09:19.160 --> 01:09:20.800
after the instruction.

01:09:20.800 --> 01:09:23.160
And then I'll put another set down here

01:09:23.160 --> 01:09:24.960
in between my example

01:09:24.960 --> 01:09:28.320
and where we're asking OpenAI to do its thing.

01:09:28.320 --> 01:09:29.600
And so all that's doing

01:09:29.600 --> 01:09:32.200
is breaking up this body of text a little bit

01:09:32.200 --> 01:09:35.960
so OpenAI can see that it's dealing with different entities,

01:09:35.960 --> 01:09:40.720
an instruction, an example, and a request to go and complete.

01:09:40.720 --> 01:09:43.720
Okay, let's hit save and see if it works.

01:09:43.720 --> 01:09:47.240
So I'm going to put in the same vegan fish cream

01:09:47.240 --> 01:09:49.560
and I'll hit generate copy.

01:09:49.560 --> 01:09:51.840
Okay, let's check out the copy we've got.

01:09:51.840 --> 01:09:54.680
So firstly, we haven't got this ordered list.

01:09:54.680 --> 01:09:56.520
There's no numbers one to six.

01:09:56.520 --> 01:09:59.400
What we've got is a body of advertising text

01:09:59.400 --> 01:10:01.400
and that is what I wanted.

01:10:01.400 --> 01:10:04.160
Secondly, I've just checked the word count of this

01:10:04.160 --> 01:10:06.800
and it's actually coming in as 63 words.

01:10:06.800 --> 01:10:11.360
Now the example that I put here is actually 54 words.

01:10:11.360 --> 01:10:14.080
So there's only nine words between the two

01:10:14.080 --> 01:10:15.800
and that is pretty good.

01:10:15.800 --> 01:10:18.000
And if we have a look down in the console,

01:10:18.000 --> 01:10:20.640
we can see that the finished reason is stop.

01:10:20.640 --> 01:10:23.200
That makes sense because this is very much

01:10:23.200 --> 01:10:25.480
the end of the sentence and the end of the text

01:10:25.480 --> 01:10:28.000
so OpenAI has given us everything

01:10:28.000 --> 01:10:29.680
that it wanted to give us.

01:10:29.680 --> 01:10:32.760
So the example is doing a really good job

01:10:32.760 --> 01:10:36.880
of allowing us to show OpenAI what it is we want.

01:10:36.880 --> 01:10:39.960
Now remember, this is called the few shot

01:10:39.960 --> 01:10:43.040
and we can add one or more examples.

01:10:43.040 --> 01:10:46.720
We should remember however, that longer prompts cost more

01:10:46.720 --> 01:10:48.760
so you don't wanna go too far.

01:10:48.760 --> 01:10:51.120
But let's go ahead and add one more example

01:10:51.120 --> 01:10:52.600
and actually this is something

01:10:52.600 --> 01:10:54.920
that you're going to do as a challenge.

01:10:54.920 --> 01:10:57.440
So let's get straight onto that in the next script.

01:11:01.400 --> 01:11:03.080
Okay, so here's your challenge.

01:11:03.080 --> 01:11:05.120
Add a second example here,

01:11:05.120 --> 01:11:08.280
be sure to make it similar in design to the first.

01:11:08.280 --> 01:11:11.920
Now I've put that because we don't want to confuse the AI.

01:11:11.920 --> 01:11:15.880
The examples that we give should be in a similar format

01:11:15.880 --> 01:11:17.600
and they should be consistent

01:11:17.600 --> 01:11:19.800
else we're just creating confusion.

01:11:19.800 --> 01:11:22.760
Now I've also put here, remember to use separators.

01:11:22.760 --> 01:11:25.440
So that is these three triple hashtags

01:11:25.440 --> 01:11:27.840
and you can use them in exactly the same way

01:11:27.840 --> 01:11:31.840
to separate out your example from the request to create.

01:11:31.840 --> 01:11:33.600
Now one thing I want you to remember here

01:11:33.600 --> 01:11:37.120
is that the law of diminishing returns applies.

01:11:37.120 --> 01:11:38.760
Adding more and more examples

01:11:38.760 --> 01:11:41.000
will not guarantee better results.

01:11:41.000 --> 01:11:43.760
You might see great results or you might not.

01:11:43.760 --> 01:11:45.320
Also before you do this challenge,

01:11:45.320 --> 01:11:46.760
I just want to say that I'm aware

01:11:46.760 --> 01:11:48.640
that some people following this course

01:11:48.640 --> 01:11:50.680
might be at a disadvantage here

01:11:50.680 --> 01:11:52.920
because English is not their first language

01:11:52.920 --> 01:11:55.920
or perhaps language is just something they struggle with.

01:11:55.920 --> 01:11:59.480
So I've added a file up here called product.md

01:11:59.480 --> 01:12:01.520
and that has got an example that you can use.

01:12:01.520 --> 01:12:03.040
So you can copy the text

01:12:03.040 --> 01:12:05.440
and just stick to practicing the layout

01:12:05.440 --> 01:12:07.480
and the syntax of the prompt.

01:12:07.480 --> 01:12:09.920
Okay, pause now, get this challenge sorted

01:12:09.920 --> 01:12:12.200
and I'll see you back here in just a minute.

01:12:15.960 --> 01:12:17.880
Okay, hopefully you got that working.

01:12:17.880 --> 01:12:19.560
So I'm just going to come in here

01:12:19.560 --> 01:12:21.560
and I'm going to copy all of the texts

01:12:21.560 --> 01:12:23.200
that I've got right here

01:12:23.200 --> 01:12:26.840
and let's just put our second example underneath the first.

01:12:26.840 --> 01:12:29.640
First thing that I want to do is separate out the examples.

01:12:29.640 --> 01:12:31.880
So we'll borrow these hashtags.

01:12:31.880 --> 01:12:34.840
Now I'm just going to take the product name

01:12:34.840 --> 01:12:38.720
and that will be solar swim, product description.

01:12:38.720 --> 01:12:41.280
It's this crazy swimming costume with solar cells

01:12:41.280 --> 01:12:42.960
to charge your phone while you're on the beach

01:12:42.960 --> 01:12:44.080
or what have you.

01:12:44.080 --> 01:12:45.800
And we've got the target market,

01:12:45.800 --> 01:12:47.560
which is of course young adults

01:12:47.560 --> 01:12:49.920
who'll spend their money on anything.

01:12:49.920 --> 01:12:52.920
Finally, we've got the advertising copy

01:12:52.920 --> 01:12:56.000
and that is approximately the same length and style

01:12:56.000 --> 01:12:59.000
as the advertising copy we've got right here.

01:12:59.000 --> 01:13:00.600
So that should do the trick.

01:13:00.600 --> 01:13:04.680
Let's just remove that space and we'll hit save.

01:13:04.680 --> 01:13:08.320
And let's give it a go and I'll hit generate copy.

01:13:08.320 --> 01:13:11.200
And okay, again, that has been pretty successful.

01:13:11.200 --> 01:13:14.280
The word count is coming in at just under 50 words.

01:13:14.280 --> 01:13:18.680
Well, our examples were 54 words and 53 words respectively.

01:13:18.680 --> 01:13:20.480
So that is pretty good.

01:13:20.480 --> 01:13:23.600
And also I think we're getting pretty decent copy.

01:13:23.600 --> 01:13:25.520
Now it can be really, really hard to judge

01:13:25.520 --> 01:13:27.720
because open AI is not going to give you

01:13:27.720 --> 01:13:30.800
the same completion for the same prompt each time.

01:13:30.800 --> 01:13:33.520
So it's really hard to judge when you refactor a prompt

01:13:33.520 --> 01:13:35.720
exactly how much difference is made.

01:13:35.720 --> 01:13:38.480
But I think two examples is a pretty good amount

01:13:38.480 --> 01:13:40.120
for this few shot approach.

01:13:40.120 --> 01:13:44.320
And it's definitely had a beneficial effect on this app.

01:13:44.320 --> 01:13:46.800
So what we need to do now is go back to the function

01:13:46.800 --> 01:13:48.360
that generates our synopsis

01:13:48.360 --> 01:13:51.880
and see if the few shot approach will improve it.

01:13:51.880 --> 01:13:54.240
When you're ready for that, let's move on.

01:13:58.120 --> 01:14:00.640
Okay, so we have this synopsis fetch request

01:14:00.640 --> 01:14:03.920
and perhaps we can tighten up the synopsis we get back

01:14:03.920 --> 01:14:07.240
and improve it by adding an example or two

01:14:07.240 --> 01:14:09.200
with a few shot approach.

01:14:09.200 --> 01:14:10.120
Now, when you do this,

01:14:10.120 --> 01:14:12.280
you're welcome to use your own examples.

01:14:12.280 --> 01:14:14.440
In fact, I would encourage you to do that.

01:14:14.440 --> 01:14:16.800
If you're going to be working with open AI,

01:14:16.800 --> 01:14:20.120
then it's important to practice creating prompts.

01:14:20.120 --> 01:14:23.640
However, I have put an example synopsis up here

01:14:23.640 --> 01:14:27.400
in synopsis.md, which you can use if you'd like to

01:14:27.400 --> 01:14:29.920
when you complete this challenge.

01:14:29.920 --> 01:14:32.720
So your challenge is to refactor this prompt

01:14:32.720 --> 01:14:35.040
to use one or more examples,

01:14:35.040 --> 01:14:37.480
just like we did in the previous script.

01:14:37.480 --> 01:14:40.000
And remember to separate out the instruction

01:14:40.000 --> 01:14:42.640
from the example with either the triple hash

01:14:42.640 --> 01:14:44.920
or the triple inverted comma.

01:14:44.920 --> 01:14:47.840
Check back if you need to remind yourself of the syntax

01:14:47.840 --> 01:14:50.360
and I'll see you back here in just a moment.

01:14:55.120 --> 01:14:58.000
Okay, hopefully you managed to do that just fine.

01:14:58.000 --> 01:14:59.840
So I'm going to come in here

01:14:59.840 --> 01:15:03.120
and we're going to rework this prompt

01:15:03.120 --> 01:15:06.560
and I'm going to replace this with the following.

01:15:06.560 --> 01:15:08.680
Generate an engaging professional

01:15:08.680 --> 01:15:12.520
and marketable movie synopsis based on an outline.

01:15:12.520 --> 01:15:14.880
Now I'll come down onto a new line.

01:15:14.880 --> 01:15:17.480
I'm going to add my hashtag separator

01:15:17.480 --> 01:15:19.960
and then I'll add my example.

01:15:19.960 --> 01:15:22.960
And my example needs an outline and a synopsis.

01:15:24.000 --> 01:15:26.680
And I'm going to use the examples I prepared earlier.

01:15:26.680 --> 01:15:31.680
This is the outline and then we'll also take the synopsis.

01:15:31.960 --> 01:15:34.680
And I've made sure that this example synopsis

01:15:34.680 --> 01:15:39.200
is the kind of thing that I want to get back from OpenAI.

01:15:39.200 --> 01:15:43.120
Now, underneath that we'll add another separator

01:15:43.120 --> 01:15:45.120
and then it's outline.

01:15:45.120 --> 01:15:46.600
And this is where we need to bring in

01:15:46.600 --> 01:15:48.320
the user generated outline.

01:15:49.520 --> 01:15:54.040
And then the synopsis, which of course we can leave blank.

01:15:54.040 --> 01:15:55.920
Okay, let's hit save.

01:15:55.920 --> 01:15:58.840
And I'm just going to pop over to the CSS

01:15:58.840 --> 01:16:01.680
and I'll just uncomment this one one more time.

01:16:01.680 --> 01:16:03.960
So we'll see the synopsis appear here

01:16:03.960 --> 01:16:07.720
and let's put in a one sentence idea.

01:16:08.640 --> 01:16:11.240
So I've gone for a madman develops a machine

01:16:11.240 --> 01:16:12.720
to control all humans

01:16:12.720 --> 01:16:16.520
and only intelligent animals can save the human race.

01:16:16.520 --> 01:16:19.760
There we're getting our long initial response.

01:16:19.760 --> 01:16:23.400
And then down here, let's just wait for the synopsis.

01:16:23.400 --> 01:16:25.360
And there it is.

01:16:25.360 --> 01:16:29.320
Okay, the first thing I want to do is check the word count.

01:16:29.320 --> 01:16:30.360
And the good news is,

01:16:30.360 --> 01:16:33.960
it's almost exactly the same length as this example.

01:16:33.960 --> 01:16:36.440
There's less than 10 words in it.

01:16:36.440 --> 01:16:38.280
Now also, and this is subjective,

01:16:38.280 --> 01:16:39.760
but if you read through it,

01:16:39.760 --> 01:16:42.560
I think this is a pretty good synopsis.

01:16:42.560 --> 01:16:44.240
To me, it seems tight.

01:16:44.240 --> 01:16:46.000
It tells the whole story.

01:16:46.000 --> 01:16:47.600
It packs a lot of detail in.

01:16:47.600 --> 01:16:49.120
There's not too much fluff.

01:16:49.120 --> 01:16:51.160
So I'm pretty happy with that.

01:16:51.160 --> 01:16:53.760
And again, as always with OpenAI,

01:16:53.760 --> 01:16:56.040
it's really hard to make a comparison.

01:16:56.040 --> 01:16:58.160
But I think adding that example to the prompt

01:16:58.160 --> 01:17:00.680
has made a big difference.

01:17:00.680 --> 01:17:03.880
Now, of course, the synopsis makes this prompt quite big.

01:17:03.880 --> 01:17:06.480
And if we were to add several examples,

01:17:06.480 --> 01:17:10.080
we could end up burning tokens here unnecessarily.

01:17:10.080 --> 01:17:12.480
So if we were gonna take this to production,

01:17:12.480 --> 01:17:16.360
maybe we would run a bunch of tests with multiple synopses

01:17:16.360 --> 01:17:19.400
and then reduce the number to the minimum needed.

01:17:19.400 --> 01:17:23.800
Now, before we move on, I have got one more challenge for you.

01:17:23.800 --> 01:17:27.200
And I'm just going to come up here and paste it in.

01:17:27.200 --> 01:17:30.320
Okay, so the initial response that we get back

01:17:30.320 --> 01:17:33.000
when we first put our one line concept

01:17:33.000 --> 01:17:35.840
into the text area is pretty long.

01:17:35.840 --> 01:17:37.560
It doesn't actually break the layout,

01:17:37.560 --> 01:17:40.040
but it does just stretch things a bit too much.

01:17:40.040 --> 01:17:42.640
And I think it's all a bit unnecessary.

01:17:42.640 --> 01:17:46.000
What I prefer is to see something like this.

01:17:46.000 --> 01:17:48.640
So we've got a good personalized response,

01:17:48.640 --> 01:17:50.960
but it's just not that long.

01:17:50.960 --> 01:17:52.760
There's just enough there to make it clear

01:17:52.760 --> 01:17:56.000
that OpenAI has understood our request

01:17:56.000 --> 01:17:58.440
and is giving us a conversational response

01:17:58.440 --> 01:18:01.920
which references the one line input from the user.

01:18:01.920 --> 01:18:04.080
So here's a challenge for you.

01:18:04.080 --> 01:18:06.000
I want you to refactor this prompt

01:18:06.000 --> 01:18:08.120
to use examples of an outline

01:18:08.120 --> 01:18:10.440
and an enthusiastic response.

