01:29:04.360 --> 01:29:07.000
But now I want to introduce a new property,

01:29:07.000 --> 01:29:09.160
which is called temperature.

01:29:09.160 --> 01:29:12.040
And we're just going to add that property right here

01:29:12.040 --> 01:29:14.880
to the object that we pass to OpenAI.

01:29:14.880 --> 01:29:17.760
Before we dive in and start using temperature,

01:29:17.760 --> 01:29:21.480
let's just have a quick bit of theory about what it does.

01:29:21.480 --> 01:29:25.160
So we know that OpenAI works by predicting the likelihood

01:29:25.160 --> 01:29:29.040
of one language chunk or token following another.

01:29:29.040 --> 01:29:31.680
So if we had a phrase like the dog,

01:29:31.680 --> 01:29:35.600
well, OpenAI could complete that as the dog was sleeping,

01:29:35.600 --> 01:29:38.200
the dog was hungry, the dog bit me.

01:29:38.200 --> 01:29:41.280
There are millions and millions of possibilities.

01:29:41.280 --> 01:29:45.320
What temperature does is it controls how often the model

01:29:45.320 --> 01:29:47.880
outputs a less likely token.

01:29:47.880 --> 01:29:50.760
So what it's doing is giving us some control

01:29:50.760 --> 01:29:54.000
over whether our completions are safe and predictable

01:29:54.000 --> 01:29:58.480
on the one hand or more creative and varied on the other hand.

01:29:58.480 --> 01:30:04.280
Now temperature is set from zero to one in increments of 0.01,

01:30:04.280 --> 01:30:06.280
although you are going to find it really hard

01:30:06.280 --> 01:30:09.280
to see the difference with small changes.

01:30:09.280 --> 01:30:12.720
Now it defaults to one, so all of the API requests

01:30:12.720 --> 01:30:15.240
we've made so far in our app have used

01:30:15.240 --> 01:30:17.720
the default temperature of one.

01:30:17.720 --> 01:30:20.640
Now lower temperatures, for example, at zero,

01:30:20.640 --> 01:30:23.480
will use fewer less likely tokens.

01:30:23.480 --> 01:30:27.560
So the completions will be less creative and more predictable.

01:30:27.560 --> 01:30:29.680
And this is absolutely great if you're looking

01:30:29.680 --> 01:30:31.280
for factual responses.

01:30:31.280 --> 01:30:35.640
Now higher temperatures will use more less likely tokens.

01:30:35.640 --> 01:30:38.040
So in doing that, you're going to get more variety

01:30:38.040 --> 01:30:39.520
and more creativity.

