is more than capable of recognizing names and brackets.

01:36:20.080 --> 01:36:23.200
But what I do want to do, though, is add an example.

01:36:23.200 --> 01:36:26.320
So I'm going to come down here onto a new line

01:36:26.320 --> 01:36:27.760
and I'll use a divider.

01:36:27.760 --> 01:36:29.960
So that will be the triple hashtag.

01:36:29.960 --> 01:36:32.160
And now I'm actually going to take the example

01:36:32.160 --> 01:36:33.520
that we've got up here.

01:36:33.520 --> 01:36:35.320
It's this Top Gun one.

01:36:35.320 --> 01:36:37.760
So we can borrow all of that.

01:36:37.760 --> 01:36:39.920
And I'll just paste it in here.

01:36:39.920 --> 01:36:42.240
Now we've got all of the names in brackets.

01:36:42.240 --> 01:36:45.520
So let's just show OpenAI what it is we're looking for.

01:36:45.520 --> 01:36:48.440
So I'll say names and then a colon.

01:36:48.440 --> 01:36:52.720
And then I'll just list out all of the names from the brackets.

01:36:52.720 --> 01:36:55.360
So Tom Cruise, Val Kilmer, and Kelly McGillis.

01:36:55.360 --> 01:36:57.840
And if we have a look back at the slide,

