And we've also got a decent synopsis.

01:37:50.400 --> 01:37:51.840
Now the final thing that we need

01:37:51.840 --> 01:37:54.760
to finish this app off is an image.

01:37:54.760 --> 01:37:56.120
But before we can do that,

01:37:56.120 --> 01:37:59.800
we need to learn about generating images with OpenAI.

01:37:59.800 --> 01:38:00.760
That's a little bit different

01:38:00.760 --> 01:38:02.360
to everything we've done so far.

01:38:02.360 --> 01:38:04.720
So let's investigate that next.

01:38:04.720 --> 01:38:09.720
Okay, let's take a look at generating images with OpenAI.

01:38:09.720 --> 01:38:13.040
So you've probably seen OpenAI's image generation tool,

01:38:13.040 --> 01:38:15.000
DALI, and if you haven't,

01:38:15.000 --> 01:38:17.160
you really should take a moment to go and play with it.

01:38:17.160 --> 01:38:19.360
This link is of course clickable.

01:38:19.360 --> 01:38:20.840
It will take you straight there.

01:38:20.840 --> 01:38:23.080
It really, really is a lot of fun.

01:38:23.080 --> 01:38:25.480
Now, as well as the DALI playground,

01:38:25.480 --> 01:38:28.720
we can access the OpenAI image API,

01:38:28.720 --> 01:38:32.080
which allows us to generate images in our application.

01:38:32.080 --> 01:38:35.320
And I'm actually building one such application right here.

01:38:35.320 --> 01:38:37.360
It's a really simple, fun game.

01:38:37.360 --> 01:38:40.520
All you have to do is describe a famous painting

01:38:40.520 --> 01:38:42.680
without saying the name of the painting

01:38:42.680 --> 01:38:44.520
or the name of the artist.

01:38:44.520 --> 01:38:46.920
So if I wanted to generate an image

01:38:46.920 --> 01:38:49.000
of the most famous painting in the world,

01:38:49.000 --> 01:38:50.640
I could say something like,

01:38:50.640 --> 01:38:52.640
a 16th century woman with long brown hair

01:38:52.640 --> 01:38:56.400
standing in front of a green vista with cloudy skies.

01:38:56.400 --> 01:38:59.840
She's looking at the viewer with a faint smile on her lips.

01:38:59.840 --> 01:39:02.800
Looking at the viewer with a faint smile on her lips.

01:39:02.800 --> 01:39:05.400
And if I give that description to OpenAI,

01:39:05.400 --> 01:39:07.880
hopefully it's going to give me a good likeness

01:39:07.880 --> 01:39:08.960
of the Mona Lisa,

01:39:08.960 --> 01:39:10.640
which is going to appear right here

01:39:10.640 --> 01:39:12.360
inside this picture frame.

01:39:12.360 --> 01:39:16.200
Now, all of these CSS and HTML for this app is already done.

01:39:16.200 --> 01:39:18.280
We just need to finish off the JavaScript

01:39:18.280 --> 01:39:20.220
and there's nothing unfamiliar happening here.

01:39:20.220 --> 01:39:22.960
The user is going to input their image description

01:39:22.960 --> 01:39:24.820
right here, click create.

01:39:24.820 --> 01:39:27.120
There's an event listener on that button

01:39:27.120 --> 01:39:29.760
and it is going to call generate image,

01:39:29.760 --> 01:39:34.400
generate image is going to call the OpenAI image API.

01:39:34.400 --> 01:39:37.540
So let's go ahead and set up a response right here.

01:39:37.540 --> 01:39:38.480
And up until now,

01:39:38.480 --> 01:39:41.880
this is where we've been using the create completion endpoint.

01:39:41.880 --> 01:39:45.420
And now we want to use the create image endpoint.

01:39:45.420 --> 01:39:47.200
Now, just like with create completion,

01:39:47.200 --> 01:39:50.680
we need to pass an object with a set of properties,

01:39:50.680 --> 01:39:53.000
but actually these are not the same properties

01:39:53.000 --> 01:39:55.700
as we've used before with create completion.

01:39:55.700 --> 01:39:57.880
We actually don't need to specify a model.

01:39:57.880 --> 01:39:59.520
We don't need to give it max tokens

01:39:59.520 --> 01:40:00.640
or temperature.

01:40:00.640 --> 01:40:02.520
Let's just have a quick look at the properties

01:40:02.520 --> 01:40:03.700
that we do need.

01:40:03.700 --> 01:40:05.920
So first up, we need a prompt.

01:40:05.920 --> 01:40:07.560
This will be a description of the image

01:40:07.560 --> 01:40:09.680
and we'll go into more detail about prompt writing

01:40:09.680 --> 01:40:11.900
for images in just a moment.

01:40:11.900 --> 01:40:15.700
The second property is N and N just stands for number

01:40:15.700 --> 01:40:18.120
and it controls the number of images

01:40:18.120 --> 01:40:20.800
we get back from OpenAI.

01:40:20.800 --> 01:40:24.400
Now we can pass it an integer between one and 10.

01:40:24.400 --> 01:40:28.160
So the maximum number of images we can get in one go is 10

01:40:28.160 --> 01:40:30.240
and it will actually default to one.

01:40:30.240 --> 01:40:33.260
So strictly speaking, I didn't need to add it here,

01:40:33.260 --> 01:40:35.880
but it's really, really important that you know it's there

01:40:35.880 --> 01:40:37.740
because in the future you might want to work

01:40:37.740 --> 01:40:39.320
with multiple images.

01:40:39.320 --> 01:40:43.440
Next up, we've got size and size takes in a string

01:40:43.440 --> 01:40:46.800
and that string is going to hold the size in pixels

01:40:46.800 --> 01:40:48.280
of the image we want.

01:40:48.280 --> 01:40:50.320
We've actually got three choices here.

01:40:50.320 --> 01:40:55.320
We can have 256 by 256, 512 by 512 or 1024 by 1024.

01:40:55.320 --> 01:41:00.320
Now the default here is the big one 1024 by 1024.

01:41:00.900 --> 01:41:04.060
And remember, bigger images cost more credit.

01:41:04.060 --> 01:41:06.980
So what you don't want to do is just always leave

01:41:06.980 --> 01:41:09.540
that at the default, take the biggest images

01:41:09.540 --> 01:41:12.860
and then resize it to something much smaller with CSS.

01:41:12.860 --> 01:41:14.780
That's really uneconomical.

01:41:14.780 --> 01:41:17.820
So just be careful to go for the image size that you want.

01:41:17.820 --> 01:41:20.480
Today we'll be going for the smaller image.

01:41:20.480 --> 01:41:24.100
And the last property we've got here is the response format

01:41:24.100 --> 01:41:26.220
and that is also a string.

01:41:26.220 --> 01:41:30.860
And the string can either be URL or B64 underscore JSON.

01:41:30.860 --> 01:41:34.380
So what this is giving us is the format of the completion.

01:41:34.380 --> 01:41:37.740
If it gives us a URL, we can just use that URL

01:41:37.740 --> 01:41:40.340
as a source inside an image element.

01:41:40.340 --> 01:41:43.020
And actually this will default to URL.

01:41:43.020 --> 01:41:44.540
And when you're doing the challenges,

01:41:44.540 --> 01:41:47.140
I recommend that you use URL.

01:41:47.140 --> 01:41:50.460
But there's a bit more we need to say about response format.

01:41:50.460 --> 01:41:54.220
Firstly, you need to be aware that OpenAI image URLs

01:41:54.220 --> 01:41:56.260
only last for one hour.

01:41:56.260 --> 01:41:59.700
So if you want to keep an image, you need to download it.

01:41:59.700 --> 01:42:00.740
As I'm recording this

01:42:00.740 --> 01:42:03.260
and my images need to last longer than an hour,

01:42:03.260 --> 01:42:07.360
I'm actually going to use this B64 underscore JSON method.

01:42:07.360 --> 01:42:10.820
And this is going to give me an encoded PNG image

01:42:10.820 --> 01:42:14.620
so I don't need to rely on OpenAI's URLs.

01:42:14.620 --> 01:42:15.820
Now, if you've never worked

01:42:15.820 --> 01:42:18.360
with a base 64 encoded image before,

01:42:18.360 --> 01:42:21.180
all it is is a massive chunk of code

01:42:21.180 --> 01:42:24.180
which the browser can interpret as an image.

01:42:24.180 --> 01:42:26.900
This is one that I've just pasted into VS code

01:42:26.900 --> 01:42:29.520
and it is absolutely huge.

01:42:29.520 --> 01:42:31.420
If you try and log this out in Scrimba,

01:42:31.420 --> 01:42:33.860
you'll likely actually crash the editor.

01:42:33.860 --> 01:42:38.180
You can search online for base 64 image to PNG conversions

01:42:38.180 --> 01:42:39.580
and you'll find plenty of sites

01:42:39.580 --> 01:42:42.140
where you can just paste in all of this code

01:42:42.140 --> 01:42:43.820
and it will just give you an image.

01:42:43.820 --> 01:42:45.340
But what's also important to know

01:42:45.340 --> 01:42:47.180
is that you can add a little bit of code

01:42:47.180 --> 01:42:49.380
just before the source in the image tag

01:42:49.380 --> 01:42:53.480
to tell the browser to expect a base 64 encoded image.

01:42:53.480 --> 01:42:56.180
And we're going to see that in just a moment.

01:42:56.180 --> 01:42:58.300
A quick word about prompt design.

01:42:58.300 --> 01:43:00.980
Prompt writing for images is actually less complex

01:43:00.980 --> 01:43:03.620
than the prompt writing we've done for text so far.

01:43:03.620 --> 01:43:07.360
All we really need to do is describe what we want in detail

01:43:07.360 --> 01:43:10.220
in a maximum of 1000 characters.

01:43:10.220 --> 01:43:11.980
Now, the more detailed the description,

01:43:11.980 --> 01:43:13.540
the more likely you are to get back

01:43:13.540 --> 01:43:14.740
the results that you want.

01:43:14.740 --> 01:43:17.980
So consider this, if you ask for a white dog,

01:43:17.980 --> 01:43:19.420
that's a bad description.

01:43:19.420 --> 01:43:21.320
You're not giving any detail at all

01:43:21.320 --> 01:43:23.100
and you're exerting no control

01:43:23.100 --> 01:43:24.980
over what you're going to get back.

01:43:24.980 --> 01:43:27.020
If on the other hand, you ask for a close-up

01:43:27.020 --> 01:43:30.300
studio photographic portrait of an old English sheepdog,

01:43:30.300 --> 01:43:32.380
well, that is a good description

01:43:32.380 --> 01:43:34.240
and then you can really start to imagine

01:43:34.240 --> 01:43:35.620
what you're going to get back

01:43:35.620 --> 01:43:37.940
and you'll actually find with that level of detail,

01:43:37.940 --> 01:43:41.300
it's quite easy to exert control over the images

01:43:41.300 --> 01:43:43.240
you get back from OpenAI.

01:43:43.240 --> 01:43:44.820
Let's get the rest of this coded out

01:43:44.820 --> 01:43:47.260
and then we can actually see it all in action.

01:43:47.260 --> 01:43:49.460
So I'm going to come in here

01:43:49.460 --> 01:43:52.220
