01:48:01.580 --> 01:48:03.940
and have our users write an image prompt.

01:48:03.940 --> 01:48:07.100
But the whole point of AI is that it's labor saving.

01:48:07.100 --> 01:48:09.020
So what we want to do is actually

01:48:09.020 --> 01:48:12.540
use the title and synopsis to generate an image prompt

01:48:12.540 --> 01:48:13.420
for us.

01:48:13.420 --> 01:48:15.780
And that is a key power of AI.

01:48:15.780 --> 01:48:17.420
You can use what you've generated

01:48:17.420 --> 01:48:19.060
to generate something else.

01:48:19.060 --> 01:48:20.900
So it's a kind of chain reaction.

01:48:20.900 --> 01:48:24.460
Now, we're going to use two functions to do this.

01:48:24.460 --> 01:48:27.220
The first function is going to generate the prompt.

01:48:27.220 --> 01:48:29.780
And the second function is going to use that prompt

01:48:29.780 --> 01:48:31.660
to generate an image.

01:48:31.660 --> 01:48:34.300
So I'm going to come down here and set up a new function

01:48:34.300 --> 01:48:36.820
called fetch image prompt.

01:48:36.820 --> 01:48:39.780
Now, fetch image prompt should take in both the title

01:48:39.780 --> 01:48:41.580
and the synopsis.

01:48:41.580 --> 01:48:43.460
And I'm going to call this function

01:48:43.460 --> 01:48:47.740
from the fetch title function that we've got right here.

01:48:47.740 --> 01:48:50.180
Fetch title takes in the synopsis.

01:48:50.180 --> 01:48:52.420
And it gets us the title.

01:48:52.420 --> 01:48:55.620
And so what I think we'll do to keep things a bit tidy

01:48:55.620 --> 01:48:59.300
is actually set up the title on a const right here,

01:48:59.300 --> 01:49:02.380
because we're actually going to use the title twice.

01:49:02.380 --> 01:49:04.220
We'll use it to update the DOM.

01:49:04.220 --> 01:49:07.300
And now we'll use it when we call the fetch image

01:49:07.300 --> 01:49:09.060
prompt function.

01:49:09.060 --> 01:49:12.020
So we'll pass in title and synopsis.

01:49:12.020 --> 01:49:14.860
OK, now before we generate any images,

01:49:14.860 --> 01:49:18.300
we should actually check in the console what prompt we get back

01:49:18.300 --> 01:49:19.740
to make sure it's good.

01:49:19.740 --> 01:49:22.020
So for now, I'm just going to log out the prompt

01:49:22.020 --> 01:49:24.100
that this function generates.

01:49:24.100 --> 01:49:27.340
And now, of course, we need to build the AI call.

