We need a Google Firebase account.

02:48:46.100 --> 02:48:47.820
So head over to the homepage

02:48:47.820 --> 02:48:50.900
and actually the image on this slide is a link.

02:48:50.900 --> 02:48:54.080
Click on it and it's going to take you straight there.

02:48:54.080 --> 02:48:56.260
When you're there, click on Get Started

02:48:56.260 --> 02:48:58.900
and that is going to take you to a signup page.

02:48:58.900 --> 02:49:00.260
And once you've entered your details

02:49:00.260 --> 02:49:01.300
and set up your account,

02:49:01.300 --> 02:49:04.460
you'll end up on a page looking like this.

02:49:04.460 --> 02:49:06.220
Click Create Project

02:49:06.220 --> 02:49:08.740
and here we need to give the project a name.

02:49:08.740 --> 02:49:11.260
I'm going for know it all dash open AI

02:49:11.260 --> 02:49:13.900
but of course you can call yours whatever you want.

02:49:13.900 --> 02:49:17.300
And now it's going to ask us if we want Google Analytics

02:49:17.300 --> 02:49:19.780
and for this project, I'm going to turn it off.

02:49:19.780 --> 02:49:21.580
Now hit Create Project

02:49:21.580 --> 02:49:23.820
and it will take a few moments to set things up.

02:49:23.820 --> 02:49:26.280
And when it's ready, you can just click Continue.

02:49:26.280 --> 02:49:29.820
Now we've created our project, go over to Build

02:49:29.820 --> 02:49:34.740
and then from the dropdown menu, select Realtime Database.

02:49:34.740 --> 02:49:36.620
Click Next, click Create Database.

02:49:36.620 --> 02:49:38.620
But if you're interested in finding out a little bit

02:49:38.620 --> 02:49:41.940
about the different types of database that Firebase offers,

02:49:41.940 --> 02:49:43.700
then do click this link

02:49:43.700 --> 02:49:45.780
and that will give you a little bit more info.

02:49:45.780 --> 02:49:48.620
For this project, we're using the Realtime Database

02:49:48.620 --> 02:49:50.960
which is the easier one to work with.

02:49:50.960 --> 02:49:53.660
So create database and then in the popup,

02:49:53.660 --> 02:49:55.860
select the server that's nearest to you.

02:49:55.860 --> 02:49:58.860
I'm in the UK, so my nearest is Belgium.

02:49:58.860 --> 02:50:00.940
Click Next and it's going to offer us

02:50:00.940 --> 02:50:02.780
locked mode or test mode.

02:50:02.780 --> 02:50:04.480
I'm going for test mode

02:50:04.480 --> 02:50:07.780
and that does mean that anybody with my database reference

02:50:07.780 --> 02:50:12.220
will be able to view, edit or delete any of my data.

02:50:12.220 --> 02:50:14.380
Now that's fine for the purposes of this course.

02:50:14.380 --> 02:50:17.100
By the time this gets published, I will have locked this down.

02:50:17.100 --> 02:50:19.060
I recommend starting in test mode.

02:50:19.060 --> 02:50:20.500
It's just a little bit easier

02:50:20.500 --> 02:50:22.400
to not have to deal with the security rules

02:50:22.400 --> 02:50:23.320
at the beginning.

02:50:23.320 --> 02:50:24.940
You can always read up on that later

02:50:24.940 --> 02:50:27.940
and make some changes to the security rules if necessary.

02:50:27.940 --> 02:50:30.580
And there we are, we have our database.

02:50:30.580 --> 02:50:33.980
And the most important thing here is this URL.

02:50:33.980 --> 02:50:36.140
That is the URL we'll be using

02:50:36.140 --> 02:50:38.460
to communicate with our database.

02:50:38.460 --> 02:50:40.580
So let me just zoom in on that.

02:50:40.580 --> 02:50:41.420
There it is.

02:50:41.420 --> 02:50:42.900
I'm going to click here to copy it

02:50:42.900 --> 02:50:44.300
and then in our code,

02:50:44.300 --> 02:50:46.860
I'm just going to create a little comment here

02:50:46.860 --> 02:50:47.940
and paste it in.

02:50:47.940 --> 02:50:49.900
And we'll use that in the next grim

02:50:49.900 --> 02:50:51.980
when we start adding the Firebase setup

02:50:51.980 --> 02:50:54.860
to this code right here in index.js.

02:50:59.660 --> 02:51:02.220
We need to add the Firebase dependency.

02:51:02.220 --> 02:51:05.140
So I'm going to come over here to the three-dot menu.

02:51:05.140 --> 02:51:07.860
And when I click on that, a menu appears

02:51:07.860 --> 02:51:10.320
and you can't actually see that in the recording,

02:51:10.320 --> 02:51:12.540
but I'm going to select add dependency

02:51:12.540 --> 02:51:13.900
and a pop-up appears

02:51:13.900 --> 02:51:16.520
and I'm just going to type in Firebase.

02:51:16.520 --> 02:51:17.840
And I'll click add

02:51:17.840 --> 02:51:20.180
and we can see that the Firebase dependency

02:51:20.180 --> 02:51:22.820
has appeared over here on the left-hand side.

02:51:22.820 --> 02:51:24.300
Now, if you're working locally,

02:51:24.300 --> 02:51:26.620
you can install this via MPM

02:51:26.620 --> 02:51:30.140
and you can check out the Firebase docs on that right here.

02:51:30.140 --> 02:51:31.900
Again, this screenshot is a link

02:51:31.900 --> 02:51:34.720
just click it to go straight through to those docs.

02:51:34.720 --> 02:51:38.420
And by the way, you can also use a CDN to work with Firebase

02:51:38.420 --> 02:51:40.340
if you prefer to do it that way.

02:51:40.340 --> 02:51:43.180
Okay, now we've got the Firebase dependency setup.

02:51:43.180 --> 02:51:45.320
We need to import some methods.

02:51:45.320 --> 02:51:47.660
So I'm going to come right up here to the top

02:51:47.660 --> 02:51:49.660
and we'll say import

02:51:49.660 --> 02:51:51.300
and then inside curly braces,

02:51:51.300 --> 02:51:54.560
I'm going to say initialize app.

02:51:54.560 --> 02:51:58.460
And we're importing that from Firebase slash app.

02:51:58.460 --> 02:52:02.860
Next, I'm going to import get database and ref.

02:52:05.300 --> 02:52:09.600
And these are coming from Firebase slash database.

02:52:09.600 --> 02:52:11.860
Okay, that's all the methods that we need.

02:52:11.860 --> 02:52:13.500
Now I'm going to come down here

02:52:13.500 --> 02:52:17.500
and set up a const called app settings.

02:52:17.500 --> 02:52:19.460
And this is going to hold an object

02:52:19.460 --> 02:52:22.140
and it's going to have one key value pair.

02:52:23.340 --> 02:52:25.660
Database URL is the key

02:52:25.660 --> 02:52:27.820
and the value will be a string

02:52:27.820 --> 02:52:32.020
containing the URL that we got when we set up the database.

02:52:32.020 --> 02:52:34.020
And we can delete that comment now.

02:52:34.020 --> 02:52:35.340
Underneath app settings,

02:52:35.340 --> 02:52:37.260
I'm going to set up another const

02:52:37.260 --> 02:52:39.760
and this one will be database.

02:52:39.760 --> 02:52:41.500
And here we'll use one of the methods

02:52:41.500 --> 02:52:44.580
that we've just imported, get database.

02:52:44.580 --> 02:52:48.780
Next, I'm going to come down here and set up a const app.

02:52:48.780 --> 02:52:51.380
And now we will use one of the methods

02:52:51.380 --> 02:52:53.120
that we just imported.

02:52:53.120 --> 02:52:56.060
So I'm going to say initialize app

02:52:56.060 --> 02:52:59.300
and I'll pass in the app settings.

02:52:59.300 --> 02:53:01.380
Now we need a const database.

02:53:02.380 --> 02:53:04.140
And again, we'll use one of the methods

02:53:04.140 --> 02:53:06.720
we just imported, get database.

02:53:07.700 --> 02:53:09.780
And we'll pass in app.

02:53:09.780 --> 02:53:11.940
And finally, we'll set up a const

02:53:11.940 --> 02:53:14.440
called conversation in database.

02:53:15.460 --> 02:53:18.540
And I've just shortened database to DB.

02:53:18.540 --> 02:53:20.940
And we'll set that equals to ref

02:53:20.940 --> 02:53:23.540
and we'll pass in database.

02:53:23.540 --> 02:53:25.220
So what we've just done there

02:53:25.220 --> 02:53:29.000
is set up a const called conversation in DB

02:53:29.000 --> 02:53:32.180
and it stores a reference to our database.

02:53:32.180 --> 02:53:36.020
And that's really important because now conversation in DB

02:53:36.020 --> 02:53:38.700
is going to be our single source of truth

02:53:38.700 --> 02:53:41.520
for the conversation we have with the chatbot.

02:53:41.520 --> 02:53:44.340
Okay, those are all the basic settings we need for now.

02:53:44.340 --> 02:53:47.740
We will add a few more methods later as we go on.

02:53:47.740 --> 02:53:49.220
Now, before we do anything else,

02:53:49.220 --> 02:53:53.620
we do need to make a few changes to the HTML and CSS.

02:53:53.620 --> 02:53:56.160
I want to add a clear button right here.

02:53:56.160 --> 02:53:59.360
So I'm going to go over to index.html

02:53:59.360 --> 02:54:02.840
and I'll come in here and just paste in the clear button.

02:54:03.740 --> 02:54:06.780
And I'll hit save and of course we've broken the CSS.

02:54:06.780 --> 02:54:09.500
So let's head over to index.css

02:54:09.500 --> 02:54:11.860
and we need to make a couple of changes.

02:54:11.860 --> 02:54:14.260
So firstly, I'm going to come down here

02:54:14.260 --> 02:54:17.580
and paste in some CSS for the new button.

02:54:17.580 --> 02:54:18.680
And as soon as I do that,

02:54:18.680 --> 02:54:21.540
you can see that things start to change over here.

02:54:21.540 --> 02:54:24.820
Now I've used the selector clear-btn

02:54:24.820 --> 02:54:27.620
and if we have a quick look back at index.html,

02:54:27.620 --> 02:54:31.040
the button has already got that class added.

02:54:31.040 --> 02:54:33.820
And the most important part of this CSS

02:54:33.820 --> 02:54:36.360
is actually this property right here,

02:54:36.360 --> 02:54:39.300
grid area clear-btn.

02:54:39.300 --> 02:54:41.940
And we're using that because the layout up here

02:54:41.940 --> 02:54:43.820
uses CSS grid.

02:54:43.820 --> 02:54:47.260
So if we come up here to the chatbot header selector,

02:54:47.260 --> 02:54:49.540
this is where we're setting display grid

02:54:49.540 --> 02:54:52.320
and we've got the grid template areas right here.

02:54:52.320 --> 02:54:56.700
And I'm going to change this dot for clear-btn.

02:54:56.700 --> 02:54:59.200
And now things are starting to come into alignment.

02:54:59.200 --> 02:55:02.580
So clear-btn is the grid area

02:55:02.580 --> 02:55:05.260
that we've got on the clear-btn selector.

02:55:05.260 --> 02:55:08.300
Now we've still got a flat edge to this button

02:55:08.300 --> 02:55:12.440
and that's because at the moment down on line 137,

02:55:12.440 --> 02:55:14.580
we are currently selecting all buttons

02:55:14.580 --> 02:55:16.900
and we've got styles set up for this submit button

02:55:16.900 --> 02:55:18.080
that we've got right here.

02:55:18.080 --> 02:55:21.100
And the submit button has a border left of zero.

02:55:21.100 --> 02:55:23.620
Now, if we go back to index.html,

02:55:23.620 --> 02:55:26.460
we've got the submit button right here

02:55:26.460 --> 02:55:31.340
and it's actually already got a CSS class of submit-btn.

02:55:31.340 --> 02:55:33.460
So how about we come over here

02:55:33.460 --> 02:55:37.260
and we replace this with the more specific selector.

02:55:37.260 --> 02:55:38.900
Okay, that has had the effect

02:55:38.900 --> 02:55:41.800
of giving us a full rounded button,

02:55:41.800 --> 02:55:43.600
which is what we want right here.

02:55:43.600 --> 02:55:46.380
Now all we need to do is bring this into alignment

02:55:46.380 --> 02:55:49.980
by coming up to the support ID selector

02:55:49.980 --> 02:55:51.620
and taking this property right here,

02:55:51.620 --> 02:55:55.380
text align right and changing it to center.

02:55:55.380 --> 02:55:57.620
Okay, now we've got it looking how we want it

02:55:57.620 --> 02:55:59.060
and we're good to move on.

02:55:59.060 --> 02:56:02.580
Next, we need to figure out how to push our user's input

02:56:02.580 --> 02:56:03.820
to the database.

02:56:09.180 --> 02:56:11.100
Right here, we're pushing our user's input

02:56:11.100 --> 02:56:12.560
to conversation array,

02:56:12.560 --> 02:56:15.620
but now we want to store the user's input in the database.

02:56:15.620 --> 02:56:18.460
That is going to be the single source of truth.

02:56:18.460 --> 02:56:20.580
So let's use Firebase's push method

02:56:20.580 --> 02:56:23.300
to push it to the database instead.

02:56:23.300 --> 02:56:24.800
To get access to the push method,

02:56:24.800 --> 02:56:27.340
we need to add it to the list of imports.

02:56:27.340 --> 02:56:31.400
So I'll come up here and add it in right there.

02:56:31.400 --> 02:56:33.940
And then back down in the event listener,

02:56:33.940 --> 02:56:35.420
let's come in here

02:56:35.420 --> 02:56:37.820
and we're going to delete conversation array.

02:56:37.820 --> 02:56:39.620
And now we've got push

02:56:39.620 --> 02:56:42.660
and that is no longer the standard JavaScript array method.

02:56:42.660 --> 02:56:44.980
That is now the Firebase push method.

02:56:44.980 --> 02:56:46.180
And what we need to pass it

02:56:46.180 --> 02:56:49.140
is the reference of the database we want to add to.

02:56:49.140 --> 02:56:52.220
And the reference to that database we've got up here,

02:56:52.220 --> 02:56:54.580
it is conversation in DB.

02:56:54.580 --> 02:56:57.420
So we'll say push and then in brackets,

02:56:57.420 --> 02:57:00.720
conversation in DB, a comma,

02:57:00.720 --> 02:57:03.300
and then the object which we want to push.

02:57:03.300 --> 02:57:06.480
And that is of course, exactly the same object.

02:57:06.480 --> 02:57:07.740
And it's as easy as that.

02:57:07.740 --> 02:57:11.140
So now let's go ahead and type something in here

02:57:11.140 --> 02:57:12.540
and we'll hit send.

02:57:12.540 --> 02:57:15.420
And let's take a look at what we've got in the database.

02:57:15.420 --> 02:57:18.060
And there we are, it has appeared.

02:57:18.060 --> 02:57:20.400
If you log into your real time database,

02:57:20.400 --> 02:57:22.360
you'll pretty much instantly see

02:57:22.360 --> 02:57:24.940
exactly what we've just pushed to the database.

02:57:24.940 --> 02:57:27.780
So we've got the content, hello, know it all,

02:57:27.780 --> 02:57:29.260
and the role of user.

02:57:29.260 --> 02:57:31.500
So that is our object.

02:57:31.500 --> 02:57:34.020
Now doing that leaves conversation array

02:57:34.020 --> 02:57:35.900
looking pretty redundant.

02:57:35.900 --> 02:57:38.260
We don't want to store our conversation here anymore,

02:57:38.260 --> 02:57:40.700
but that leaves us with an issue.

02:57:40.700 --> 02:57:43.460
We've got this instruction object

02:57:43.460 --> 02:57:44.940
and we need to keep it somewhere.

02:57:44.940 --> 02:57:46.260
But storing it in the database

02:57:46.260 --> 02:57:47.620
with the rest of the conversation

02:57:47.620 --> 02:57:49.580
has actually got two disadvantages.

02:57:49.580 --> 02:57:52.780
Number one, if we ever want to edit the instruction

02:57:52.780 --> 02:57:55.740
to change the chatbots personality or behavior,

02:57:55.740 --> 02:57:58.900
we'll actually have to edit the database directly.

02:57:58.900 --> 02:58:01.900
And number two, when we want to clear the conversation,

02:58:01.900 --> 02:58:04.180
we're going to get caught up in JavaScript spaghetti

02:58:04.180 --> 02:58:06.720
making sure we don't delete the instruction,

02:58:06.720 --> 02:58:08.260
but do delete everything else.

02:58:08.260 --> 02:58:10.480
So we'll be making work for ourselves.

02:58:10.480 --> 02:58:12.580
The solution that I think is best

02:58:12.580 --> 02:58:15.740
is that we keep the instruction right here in index.js

02:58:15.740 --> 02:58:18.860
where it's easily accessible and easily editable,

02:58:18.860 --> 02:58:20.260
and we just add it to the array

02:58:20.260 --> 02:58:23.580
we're sending to OpenAI with each request.

02:58:23.580 --> 02:58:26.600
So what I'm going to do is change conversation array

02:58:26.600 --> 02:58:29.020
to instruction object.

02:58:29.020 --> 02:58:32.680
And now it's an object, let's delete the square brackets.

02:58:32.680 --> 02:58:34.420
And when we update fetch reply,

02:58:34.420 --> 02:58:39.180
we'll add this to the array we send off to the OpenAI API.

02:58:39.180 --> 02:58:41.660
And actually updating fetch reply

02:58:41.660 --> 02:58:43.780
is what we need to come on to next.

02:58:49.300 --> 02:58:50.660
The next thing we need to do

02:58:50.660 --> 02:58:52.900
is make some changes to fetch reply.

02:58:52.900 --> 02:58:55.340
We know we need to send the entire conversation

02:58:55.340 --> 02:58:58.700
with every request to the OpenAI API.

02:58:58.700 --> 02:59:01.340
But now that the conversation's stored on the database,

02:59:01.340 --> 02:59:03.740
we need to fetch it before we can include it

02:59:03.740 --> 02:59:05.340
with our request.

02:59:05.340 --> 02:59:08.820
And with Firebase, we do that with the get method.

02:59:08.820 --> 02:59:10.580
But before we can use the get method,

02:59:10.580 --> 02:59:13.600
we need to add it to our list of imports.

02:59:13.600 --> 02:59:17.460
So let's come up here and we'll just put it after push.

02:59:17.460 --> 02:59:20.540
Now get is a method, so we'll give it the brackets

02:59:20.540 --> 02:59:23.780
and we're going to pass in the reference to our database,

02:59:23.780 --> 02:59:26.260
just like we did with the push method.

02:59:26.260 --> 02:59:28.580
Now we're going to chain a then

02:59:28.580 --> 02:59:30.940
and here we'll have a callback function

02:59:30.940 --> 02:59:34.380
and that function gets a parameter snapshot.

02:59:34.380 --> 02:59:37.140
And snapshot is the data in our database

02:59:37.140 --> 02:59:39.380
as it exists at this time.

02:59:39.380 --> 02:59:41.280
Now inside the body of this function,

02:59:41.280 --> 02:59:43.220
let's be safe and use an if

02:59:43.220 --> 02:59:46.180
just to make sure a snapshot exists.

02:59:46.180 --> 02:59:49.300
So if, for example, writing to the database right here

02:59:49.300 --> 02:59:51.080
in the event listener failed,

02:59:51.080 --> 02:59:53.080
then we would want to know about that.

02:59:53.080 --> 02:59:56.940
So let's just say else, no data available.

02:59:56.940 --> 03:00:00.240
Because if what we send to the OpenAI API

03:00:00.240 --> 03:00:03.320
is not the array of objects it expects,

03:00:03.320 --> 03:00:05.180
it's going to give us an error anyway.

03:00:05.180 --> 03:00:08.140
So it's a good idea to check what's going on here.

03:00:08.140 --> 03:00:12.100
Now in here, we can make our request to the OpenAI API.

03:00:12.100 --> 03:00:15.420
So let's just cut and paste all of this code.

03:00:15.420 --> 03:00:17.540
And let's just format that nicely.

03:00:17.540 --> 03:00:20.220
Now we're actually not quite ready to call the API.

03:00:20.220 --> 03:00:24.000
So I'm actually going to comment out all of that code.

03:00:24.000 --> 03:00:27.260
And let's just come in here and log out snapshot.

03:00:27.260 --> 03:00:30.420
Now remember, we've already got something in our database.

03:00:30.420 --> 03:00:32.300
So there should be something for us to log out.

03:00:32.300 --> 03:00:34.700
So rather than write anything more in here

03:00:34.700 --> 03:00:36.340
and add to the database,

03:00:36.340 --> 03:00:39.260
I'm just going to call the fetch reply function.

03:00:39.260 --> 03:00:42.920
Now when I hit save, let's just see what we log out.

03:00:42.920 --> 03:00:43.760
Well, there we are.

03:00:43.760 --> 03:00:46.140
We can see the contents of our database.

03:00:46.140 --> 03:00:47.360
We've got an object.

03:00:47.360 --> 03:00:49.820
It's got a content key with hello know it all

03:00:49.820 --> 03:00:51.840
and a role key with user.

03:00:51.840 --> 03:00:52.680
But at the beginning,

03:00:52.680 --> 03:00:55.720
it's also got a Firebase identifier of some kind.

03:00:55.720 --> 03:00:58.700
And we don't want to be sending that to OpenAI.

03:00:58.700 --> 03:01:00.380
It would just really confuse it.

03:01:00.380 --> 03:01:02.540
All we want is an array of objects.

03:01:02.540 --> 03:01:05.060
So let's check what the Firebase docs say.

03:01:05.060 --> 03:01:08.660
And they talk about this val method and it says here,

03:01:08.660 --> 03:01:12.940
it extracts a JavaScript value from a data snapshot.

03:01:12.940 --> 03:01:14.980
Well, that is exactly what we want to do.

03:01:14.980 --> 03:01:16.860
Now, if you'd like to read up more about val

03:01:16.860 --> 03:01:20.100
in the Firebase docs, this screenshot is a link.

03:01:20.100 --> 03:01:22.900
So just click on it and it will take you straight there.

