03:15:12.000 --> 03:15:14.420
And look, it's telling us that it cannot recall

03:15:14.420 --> 03:15:17.820
any past interactions with us from separate sessions.

03:15:17.820 --> 03:15:19.980
And that proves that this is working.

03:15:19.980 --> 03:15:23.820
The start over button is doing exactly what we want it to.

03:15:23.820 --> 03:15:25.660
Okay, so that is a really good job.

03:15:25.660 --> 03:15:28.380
Congratulations on getting to the end of this project.

03:15:28.380 --> 03:15:31.620
Let's just take one last grim to recap what we've done

03:15:31.620 --> 03:15:33.620
and talk about where we go from here.

03:15:36.860 --> 03:15:40.700
Congratulations on finishing the know-it-all chatbot app.

03:15:40.700 --> 03:15:43.180
Now you have got the foundations you need

03:15:43.180 --> 03:15:47.420
to build any human language capable chatbot that you want.

03:15:47.420 --> 03:15:49.940
Let's just recap what we've studied.

03:15:49.940 --> 03:15:52.460
We have used the GPT-4 model

03:15:52.460 --> 03:15:55.820
and the create chat completions endpoint.

03:15:55.820 --> 03:15:57.900
We've given our chatbot a personality

03:15:57.900 --> 03:15:59.740
via the instruction object.

03:15:59.740 --> 03:16:02.500
We've seen how we can use the presence penalty setting

03:16:02.500 --> 03:16:05.740
to encourage the chatbot to talk about new topics.

03:16:05.740 --> 03:16:07.480
And we've used frequency penalty

03:16:07.480 --> 03:16:09.680
to control how repetitive the chatbot is

03:16:09.680 --> 03:16:13.220
when it selects words and phrases to use.

03:16:13.220 --> 03:16:16.180
We saved our conversation as a single source of truth

03:16:16.180 --> 03:16:19.700
in a database so the conversation can be persisted

03:16:19.700 --> 03:16:21.580
and the user can come back to it

03:16:21.580 --> 03:16:23.860
and pick it up at a later date.

03:16:23.860 --> 03:16:25.180
Now it's always a good idea

03:16:25.180 --> 03:16:27.140
to really make a project your own.

03:16:27.140 --> 03:16:30.740
So why don't you give the bot a specific function?

03:16:30.740 --> 03:16:32.060
So you could tweak the AI

03:16:32.060 --> 03:16:34.980
so that it has a specific purpose.

03:16:34.980 --> 03:16:38.660
This tech doesn't have to be a general purpose chatbot.

03:16:38.660 --> 03:16:42.380
It could be a coding expert, a poetry generator,

03:16:42.380 --> 03:16:43.820
an academic assistant.

03:16:43.820 --> 03:16:45.540
You could use the instruction object

03:16:45.540 --> 03:16:47.140
to train it to provide text

03:16:47.140 --> 03:16:49.940
in the specific style and format you need

03:16:49.940 --> 03:16:52.420
for writing reports at work, for example.

03:16:52.420 --> 03:16:54.620
The only limit is your imagination.

03:16:54.620 --> 03:16:55.960
And once you've done that,

03:16:55.960 --> 03:16:58.120
you could change the style and theme

03:16:58.120 --> 03:17:01.060
so it matches the chatbot's new purpose.

03:17:01.060 --> 03:17:02.740
And of course, it's always a good idea

03:17:02.740 --> 03:17:04.340
to build again from scratch.

03:17:04.340 --> 03:17:05.740
And if you don't need practice

03:17:05.740 --> 03:17:08.180
with the HTML, CSS, and JavaScript,

03:17:08.180 --> 03:17:10.920
you could just rebuild the API specific parts

03:17:10.920 --> 03:17:14.300
to really get that syntax to stick in your brain.

03:17:14.300 --> 03:17:17.540
It would also be good to add some error handling.

03:17:17.540 --> 03:17:19.980
We haven't really looked at error handling in this course.

03:17:19.980 --> 03:17:22.380
