03:17:22.380 --> 03:17:24.660
But whenever you're working with APIs,

03:17:24.660 --> 03:17:27.260
error handling is more than a good idea.

03:17:27.260 --> 03:17:28.540
It's essential really

03:17:28.540 --> 03:17:30.240
if you're taking anything to production.

03:17:30.240 --> 03:17:33.760
So do do a bit of research on that.

03:17:33.760 --> 03:17:36.580
But whatever you do, remember to take a break.

03:17:36.580 --> 03:17:38.860
Take a bit of time to consolidate what you've learned

03:17:38.860 --> 03:17:43.860
before moving on to the next project.

03:17:44.540 --> 03:17:46.020
Okay, so we are going to enter

03:17:46.020 --> 03:17:48.660
the fantastic world of fine tuning.

03:17:48.660 --> 03:17:52.500
And I've put here making AI models work for us.

03:17:52.500 --> 03:17:55.100
So what exactly do I mean by that?

03:17:55.100 --> 03:17:56.700
Well, in earlier projects,

03:17:56.700 --> 03:17:59.060
we have used two types of prompt.

03:17:59.060 --> 03:18:00.740
We've used the zero shot

03:18:00.740 --> 03:18:04.220
where we just give an instruction or ask a question.

03:18:04.220 --> 03:18:06.700
We've also used the few shot approach

03:18:06.700 --> 03:18:07.960
where we give an instruction

03:18:07.960 --> 03:18:11.100
and we use examples to demonstrate what we're looking for.

03:18:11.100 --> 03:18:13.700
Now those work fine for our purposes,

03:18:13.700 --> 03:18:16.660
but they have two big drawbacks.

03:18:16.660 --> 03:18:19.620
Firstly, prompts have size limits.

03:18:19.620 --> 03:18:22.780
We're limited in how much we can include in a prompt.

03:18:22.780 --> 03:18:25.620
Secondly, larger prompts use more tokens,

03:18:25.620 --> 03:18:28.120
so will be expensive when scaled.

03:18:28.120 --> 03:18:31.180
But there's actually a bigger problem than that.

03:18:31.180 --> 03:18:33.580
OpenAI's models have been trained on text

03:18:33.580 --> 03:18:35.860
openly available on the internet.

03:18:35.860 --> 03:18:38.220
Now that's great for when you want to use them

03:18:38.220 --> 03:18:41.020
for creativity, general Q&amp;A,

03:18:41.020 --> 03:18:43.100
like we've been doing with our chatbot,

03:18:43.100 --> 03:18:46.840
translation and many other general tasks as well.

03:18:46.840 --> 03:18:49.740
But what it's not good for is answering questions

03:18:49.740 --> 03:18:52.300
that are specific to your circumstances.

03:18:52.300 --> 03:18:54.700
So consider this, you have a company

03:18:54.700 --> 03:18:57.820
and that company has specific policies and systems.

03:18:57.820 --> 03:18:59.820
So you have your own opening hours,

03:18:59.820 --> 03:19:03.020
you might have shipping fees, a returns policy,

03:19:03.020 --> 03:19:05.060
of course you'll have contact details

03:19:05.060 --> 03:19:07.500
and many other things besides.

03:19:07.500 --> 03:19:10.740
Now imagine you ask a chatbot like the one we just made,

03:19:10.740 --> 03:19:13.300
a specific question about your company.

03:19:13.300 --> 03:19:15.260
What are you going to get back?

03:19:15.260 --> 03:19:18.560
Well, you're going to get hallucinations.

03:19:18.560 --> 03:19:20.220
And what are hallucinations?

03:19:20.220 --> 03:19:23.060
Well, if the AI doesn't know the answer,

03:19:23.060 --> 03:19:27.460
it gives you a linguistically plausible incorrect answer.

03:19:27.460 --> 03:19:30.460
So it basically goes into the world of fantasy.

03:19:30.460 --> 03:19:32.000
Now, although they're improving,

03:19:32.000 --> 03:19:35.380
AI models are not that good at saying, I don't know.

03:19:35.380 --> 03:19:38.340
Remember, what these models do is predict the likelihood

03:19:38.340 --> 03:19:41.380
of a token or language chunk coming next.

03:19:41.380 --> 03:19:43.300
And this is one of the biggest problems with AI

03:19:43.300 --> 03:19:44.580
when working with facts.

03:19:44.580 --> 03:19:47.300
So if I ask what my company's opening hours are,

03:19:47.300 --> 03:19:50.060
it will likely say something like 9 a.m. to 5 p.m.

03:19:50.060 --> 03:19:51.300
and close on Sundays,

03:19:51.300 --> 03:19:53.980
just because that is a plausible answer.

03:19:53.980 --> 03:19:57.260
Now, fine tuning can help with this problem.

03:19:57.260 --> 03:19:59.460
By uploading your own dataset,

03:19:59.460 --> 03:20:01.780
you can give the model the information it needs

03:20:01.780 --> 03:20:04.780
to answer questions specific to your situation.

03:20:04.780 --> 03:20:05.820
So let's go.

03:20:05.820 --> 03:20:07.540
And we're going to start by thinking about

03:20:07.540 --> 03:20:09.420
how we can convert our chatbot,

03:20:09.420 --> 03:20:11.660
which we still have all of the code for right here,

03:20:11.660 --> 03:20:14.740
into a finely tuned support bot for my new company.

03:20:14.740 --> 03:20:17.000
So let's check that out next.

