but this is for demonstration purposes.

03:35:20.980 --> 03:35:22.940
So it's absolutely fine.

03:35:22.940 --> 03:35:26.020
Now I'm going to save you reading the rest of this text here

03:35:26.020 --> 03:35:28.940
because actually it's telling us something we already know.

03:35:28.940 --> 03:35:30.780
We talked about the format of our data

03:35:30.780 --> 03:35:32.640
and all of the features that we need.

03:35:32.640 --> 03:35:36.220
And we know that we need a separator to inform the model

03:35:36.220 --> 03:35:38.380
when the prompt ends and the completion begins.

03:35:38.380 --> 03:35:40.460
We know that each completion needs to start

03:35:40.460 --> 03:35:41.980
with a single white space.

03:35:41.980 --> 03:35:43.780
And we know that each completion should end

03:35:43.780 --> 03:35:46.100
with a stop sequence to inform the model

03:35:46.100 --> 03:35:48.660
when the completion has ended.

03:35:48.660 --> 03:35:51.080
But this tool is great because it's basically going

03:35:51.080 --> 03:35:53.020
