and completion key to each pair.

03:36:52.820 --> 03:36:56.700
It's added white space before the start of every completion.

03:36:56.700 --> 03:36:58.480
It's added a new line character

03:36:58.480 --> 03:37:00.460
at the end of every completion.

03:37:00.460 --> 03:37:02.660
And of course it's added a separator

03:37:02.660 --> 03:37:04.780
at the end of every prompt.

03:37:04.780 --> 03:37:06.460
And we could have done all of that by hand

03:37:06.460 --> 03:37:08.020
and just used the tool to check,

03:37:08.020 --> 03:37:11.740
but wow, what a lot of boring work that would have been.

