to stop generating tokens at a given point.

03:53:02.940 --> 03:53:06.660
The completion will never contain the stop sequence

03:53:06.660 --> 03:53:09.440
and the stop sequence is an array.

03:53:09.440 --> 03:53:11.660
And that's because we can have multiple stops

03:53:11.660 --> 03:53:13.020
in a stop sequence.

03:53:13.020 --> 03:53:14.740
Now all of that is quite theoretical.

03:53:14.740 --> 03:53:16.720
So let's just jump straight into an example

03:53:16.720 --> 03:53:18.700
and you'll see what I mean.

03:53:18.700 --> 03:53:22.200
Right here, I've got a basic API request set up

03:53:22.200 --> 03:53:25.140
using the text DaVinci 003 model.

03:53:25.140 --> 03:53:27.700
And I'm just asking it to list some great books

03:53:27.700 --> 03:53:29.640
to read on the topic of coding.

03:53:29.640 --> 03:53:33.480
So I will uncomment this function call and hit save

03:53:33.480 --> 03:53:36.700
and let's open up the console and see what we get.

03:53:36.700 --> 03:53:40.420
And there we are, we get 10 good book recommendations.

03:53:40.420 --> 03:53:43.180
Now I'm going to come in here underneath the max tokens

03:53:43.180 --> 03:53:45.220
and I'm going to add a stop sequence

03:53:45.220 --> 03:53:48.300
and the property that we want is just stop.

03:53:48.300 --> 03:53:50.300
The stop sequence is an array

03:53:50.300 --> 03:53:53.680
and each individual stop will be a string.

03:53:53.680 --> 03:53:56.300
Now we can have up to four stops in this array.

03:53:56.300 --> 03:53:57.980
I'm only going to use one.

03:53:57.980 --> 03:54:00.920
And if we look at the formatting of what's in the console,

03:54:00.920 --> 03:54:05.140
each list item starts with a number and a dot.

03:54:05.140 --> 03:54:06.580
So it's one dot,

03:54:06.580 --> 03:54:09.180
code the hidden language of computer hardware and software

03:54:09.180 --> 03:54:10.740
by Charles Petzold,

03:54:10.740 --> 03:54:14.060
two dot, Python crash course by Eric Maths.

03:54:14.060 --> 03:54:16.900
So the stop that I put in here just to experiment with

03:54:16.900 --> 03:54:18.700
is going to be two dots.

03:54:18.700 --> 03:54:21.500
Let's see what happens when I press save.

03:54:21.500 --> 03:54:25.240
We get a list with only one item.

03:54:25.240 --> 03:54:26.820
So what happened here?

03:54:26.820 --> 03:54:28.660
Well, if you'll remember,

03:54:28.660 --> 03:54:31.660
the completion will not contain the stop sequence.

03:54:31.660 --> 03:54:35.200
So the model was prevented from writing two dots.

03:54:35.200 --> 03:54:37.420
And because it won't write a stop sequence,

03:54:37.420 --> 03:54:40.180
at that point, the completion is cut off.

03:54:40.180 --> 03:54:42.640
So if we wanted a list of five books,

03:54:42.640 --> 03:54:45.580
we could change this to six dot.

03:54:45.580 --> 03:54:48.660
And there we are, we have got a list of five books.

03:54:48.660 --> 03:54:50.980
Now you can use anything as a stop.

03:54:50.980 --> 03:54:53.020
You can put whatever characters in there

03:54:53.020 --> 03:54:54.980
you might find in your completion,

03:54:54.980 --> 03:54:57.240
but you just need to know what you're doing with it.

03:54:57.240 --> 03:55:00.380
Obviously, if you put something like the letter A,

03:55:00.380 --> 03:55:03.700
well, that's going to cause all sorts of problems.

03:55:03.700 --> 03:55:04.540
There we are.

03:55:04.540 --> 03:55:05.900
The completion has actually been cut off

03:55:05.900 --> 03:55:08.040
on the fourth letter of the book title,

03:55:08.040 --> 03:55:09.600
which was obviously an A.

03:55:09.600 --> 03:55:11.260
Now, when we're working with chat bots,

03:55:11.260 --> 03:55:14.220
it's very common to use the new line value

03:55:14.220 --> 03:55:16.140
as a stop sequence.

03:55:16.140 --> 03:55:16.980
Why?

03:55:16.980 --> 03:55:18.940
Because often you want the bot to give you

03:55:18.940 --> 03:55:21.440
one paragraph as an answer,

03:55:21.440 --> 03:55:24.180
and then you want the user to respond.

03:55:24.180 --> 03:55:26.900
If you don't use a stop sequence with a chat bot,

03:55:26.900 --> 03:55:28.820
you run the risk of the chat bot answering

03:55:28.820 --> 03:55:32.180
and asking questions and having a conversation with itself

03:55:32.180 --> 03:55:35.140
that becomes ever more bizarre and illogical

03:55:35.140 --> 03:55:38.140
until it hits the token limit and that stops it.

03:55:38.140 --> 03:55:41.820
Now with the general purpose chat bot we built with GPT-4,

03:55:41.820 --> 03:55:44.740
we didn't need to add a stop property

03:55:44.740 --> 03:55:48.020
because GPT-4 has actually got that specific syntax,

03:55:48.020 --> 03:55:51.260
the object with the role and the content properties.

03:55:51.260 --> 03:55:53.700
DaVinci and other models don't have that,

03:55:53.700 --> 03:55:56.820
so we can use the new line character as a stop

03:55:56.820 --> 03:56:00.300
to stop the bot from continuing the conversation on its own.

03:56:00.300 --> 03:56:03.660
Okay, let's go back to the app and add a stop property.

03:56:06.980 --> 03:56:09.100
Okay, so if we refer back to our slide,

03:56:09.100 --> 03:56:11.300
we can see that each completion should end

03:56:11.300 --> 03:56:13.780
with a stop sequence to inform the model

03:56:13.780 --> 03:56:15.860
when the completion ends.

03:56:15.860 --> 03:56:18.380
And when we were preparing our data,

03:56:18.380 --> 03:56:20.740
we actually selected this option

03:56:20.740 --> 03:56:23.900
to add a suffix ending of a new line character,

03:56:23.900 --> 03:56:25.880
which is backslash N.

03:56:25.880 --> 03:56:28.580
So as we add completions to our conversation,

03:56:28.580 --> 03:56:31.540
we need to include this new line character at the end

03:56:31.540 --> 03:56:33.500
as a stop sequence.

03:56:33.500 --> 03:56:36.140
Now we're also using this arrow as a separator,

03:56:36.140 --> 03:56:37.980
and when experimenting with this,

03:56:37.980 --> 03:56:41.100
I sometimes found arrows popping up in completions

03:56:41.100 --> 03:56:42.900
and some cases where the chat bot seemed

03:56:42.900 --> 03:56:45.340
to just get into a conversation with itself,

03:56:45.340 --> 03:56:48.320
asking itself questions and giving itself answers.

03:56:48.320 --> 03:56:50.700
So we're actually going to add the arrow

03:56:50.700 --> 03:56:52.640
as a stop sequence as well,

03:56:52.640 --> 03:56:55.620
because we never want the model to generate an arrow.

03:56:55.620 --> 03:56:59.140
Okay, so here is your challenge and it comes in two parts.

03:56:59.140 --> 03:57:01.740
Firstly, I want you to add the new line character,

03:57:01.740 --> 03:57:06.740
which is backslash N and the separator as a stop sequence.

03:57:06.820 --> 03:57:08.920
And actually, you don't need to have a space

03:57:08.920 --> 03:57:10.260
in the stop sequence.

03:57:10.260 --> 03:57:11.620
Secondly, I've said here,

03:57:11.620 --> 03:57:14.080
I want you to add something to the line below

03:57:14.080 --> 03:57:16.560
where we update conversation string.

03:57:16.560 --> 03:57:19.540
So that is this line of code right here.

03:57:19.540 --> 03:57:21.340
I'm going to leave you to think about that.

03:57:21.340 --> 03:57:23.860
What would it be good to add to that line?

03:57:23.860 --> 03:57:26.440
Okay, pause now, get that challenge sorted,

03:57:26.440 --> 03:57:28.660
and I'll see you back here in just a moment.

03:57:35.580 --> 03:57:38.500
Okay, so hopefully you managed to do that just fine.

03:57:38.500 --> 03:57:41.780
So let's come in here and we'll add our stop.

03:57:41.780 --> 03:57:43.800
And we know that that will be an array

03:57:43.800 --> 03:57:45.340
and it will be an array of strings.

03:57:45.340 --> 03:57:49.000
So the first string is going to be the new line character,

03:57:49.000 --> 03:57:52.260
and the second string will be the arrow separator.

03:57:52.260 --> 03:57:55.440
And of course, it doesn't matter what order they go in.

03:57:55.440 --> 03:57:56.880
Now, the second challenge,

03:57:56.880 --> 03:57:58.340
add something to the line below

03:57:58.340 --> 03:58:00.540
where we update conversation string.

03:58:00.540 --> 03:58:03.180
Well, if we refer back to this slide,

03:58:03.180 --> 03:58:06.260
we're going to add a suffix ending of backslash N

03:58:06.260 --> 03:58:08.100
to all completions.

03:58:08.100 --> 03:58:12.140
So this is the completion that we're getting back.

03:58:12.140 --> 03:58:15.460
Let's just add a new line character to the end of that.

03:58:15.460 --> 03:58:16.740
And what that is going to do

03:58:16.740 --> 03:58:18.660
is make it really clear to the model

03:58:18.660 --> 03:58:20.860
when it reads conversation string

03:58:20.860 --> 03:58:23.420
that it has reached the end of a completion

03:58:23.420 --> 03:58:26.260
because that is what the new line character will tell it.

03:58:26.260 --> 03:58:28.100
And likewise, the arrow separator

03:58:28.100 --> 03:58:30.220
that we're adding to the stop sequence here,

03:58:30.220 --> 03:58:33.580
which we're already adding to conversation string

03:58:33.580 --> 03:58:37.020
right here in the event listeners anonymous function,

03:58:37.020 --> 03:58:38.580
that will tell the model

03:58:38.580 --> 03:58:41.580
that it's reached the end of a prompt.

03:58:41.580 --> 03:58:44.260
Okay, let's hit save and see if it's worked.

