I don't know, it prefers to hallucinate.

04:05:24.520 --> 04:05:27.360
But we've effectively given it permission to do that.

04:05:27.360 --> 04:05:30.380
So do bear that in mind when working with chatbot data,

04:05:30.380 --> 04:05:33.160
it's good to teach it to say, I don't know,

04:05:33.160 --> 04:05:36.060
as this will help stop it hallucinating.

04:05:36.060 --> 04:05:38.260
Let's just ask a few more questions.

04:05:38.260 --> 04:05:41.180
So I'm going to say, how much is insurance?

04:05:43.760 --> 04:05:46.660
And it's telling me it's three pounds 75 per delivery.

04:05:46.660 --> 04:05:50.860
And if I come up onto line eight, well, there we are.

04:05:50.860 --> 04:05:54.980
It says it's a flat rate of three pounds 75 per drone order.

04:05:54.980 --> 04:05:57.440
So again, that is pretty good.

04:05:57.440 --> 04:05:59.820
Let's ask it something a little bit more random.

04:06:00.940 --> 04:06:03.460
I've said your drone crashed into my house.

04:06:04.680 --> 04:06:06.800
Okay, it says, please contact us by email

04:06:06.800 --> 04:06:08.780
and we'll arrange to pay for any damage.

04:06:08.780 --> 04:06:10.900
I'm going to say, I want compensation.

04:06:14.100 --> 04:06:14.940
And there we are.

04:06:14.940 --> 04:06:17.400
It's giving a very logical rational answer.

04:06:17.400 --> 04:06:19.700
Now it's not being particularly humane.

04:06:19.700 --> 04:06:21.600
It's not being touchy feely.

04:06:21.600 --> 04:06:23.540
It's not being that conversational.

04:06:23.540 --> 04:06:26.960
And that, to be honest, is a shortcoming of our data.

04:06:26.960 --> 04:06:29.080
We just need much, much more data.

04:06:29.080 --> 04:06:31.940
And we need much more of this kind of data

04:06:31.940 --> 04:06:33.480
that we've got at the bottom,

04:06:33.480 --> 04:06:36.120
where we've got these entire conversations

04:06:36.120 --> 04:06:38.540
playing out before we get to the completion,

04:06:38.540 --> 04:06:40.700
because that is the quality data.

04:06:40.700 --> 04:06:44.600
That's what really helps the chatbot communicate well.

04:06:44.600 --> 04:06:47.000
So although I think we've done very well here,

04:06:47.000 --> 04:06:51.060
you will find limitations with this chatbot quite quickly.

04:06:51.060 --> 04:06:53.180
You're going to come across idiosyncrasies

04:06:53.180 --> 04:06:54.840
and hallucinations.

04:06:54.840 --> 04:06:56.500
But as I've said many times,

04:06:56.500 --> 04:06:58.560
if you wanted to take this to production,

04:06:58.560 --> 04:07:01.120
you would need a lot more data.

04:07:01.120 --> 04:07:04.140
But what we've done here has really proved the principle.

04:07:04.140 --> 04:07:07.120
It's working really well on a really small data set,

04:07:07.120 --> 04:07:08.880
so that is really good.

04:07:08.880 --> 04:07:10.880
And of course, your results might differ.

04:07:10.880 --> 04:07:12.840
Perhaps you're using your own data,

04:07:12.840 --> 04:07:16.320
or perhaps the model has simply been updated somewhat

04:07:16.320 --> 04:07:18.280
between the time that this was recorded

04:07:18.280 --> 04:07:20.680
and the time that you're actually building this app.

04:07:20.680 --> 04:07:22.260
And that is the nature of working

04:07:22.260 --> 04:07:24.740
with this new frontier in technology.

04:07:24.740 --> 04:07:27.500
Now the next thing that I want to do is take this app

04:07:27.500 --> 04:07:29.460
and deploy it live on the internet

04:07:29.460 --> 04:07:31.740
with the API key safely hidden.

04:07:31.740 --> 04:07:32.900
That's quite a process.

04:07:32.900 --> 04:07:34.400
We've got quite a bit to do.

04:07:34.400 --> 04:07:36.660
So let's make a start next.

04:07:40.200 --> 04:07:43.380
Okay, so our mission is to deploy our support bot,

04:07:43.380 --> 04:07:45.340
but keep the API key hidden.

04:07:45.340 --> 04:07:48.100
And we're going to do this using Netlify.

04:07:48.100 --> 04:07:50.720
So right now, if we were just to deploy this

04:07:50.720 --> 04:07:52.800
as a front-end only project,

04:07:52.800 --> 04:07:56.080
the API key would be visible right there

04:07:56.080 --> 04:07:59.400
on every user's machine and easily obtainable

04:07:59.400 --> 04:08:02.280
from the DevTools network tab.

04:08:02.280 --> 04:08:03.940
Let's just zoom in.

04:08:03.940 --> 04:08:05.420
Oops, there it is.

04:08:05.420 --> 04:08:08.520
Our API key is there for all to see.

04:08:08.520 --> 04:08:10.420
And that is what we need to avoid.

04:08:10.420 --> 04:08:12.300
What we want is for you to be able

04:08:12.300 --> 04:08:15.140
to share the projects you've made with OpenAI

04:08:15.140 --> 04:08:17.940
without fear of your key being compromised.

04:08:17.940 --> 04:08:20.180
And actually, the process we're about to go through

04:08:20.180 --> 04:08:23.860
can be used anytime you need to keep an API key hidden.

04:08:23.860 --> 04:08:26.680
It's not specific to OpenAI in any way.

04:08:27.620 --> 04:08:29.220
So how are we going to do this?

04:08:29.220 --> 04:08:32.100
Well, let's take a high-level overview.

04:08:32.100 --> 04:08:35.300
Now, at the moment, we've got a front-end project,

04:08:35.300 --> 04:08:38.580
and what we've been doing is storing the API key

04:08:38.580 --> 04:08:42.900
on the front-end, making a request to the OpenAI API,

04:08:42.900 --> 04:08:46.060
and getting back a completion that we use on the front-end.

04:08:46.060 --> 04:08:48.140
But now, we're going to stop doing that

04:08:48.140 --> 04:08:50.040
and do something completely different.

04:08:50.040 --> 04:08:51.800
We are going to send our request

04:08:51.800 --> 04:08:54.360
to a Netlify serverless function.

04:08:54.360 --> 04:08:57.780
The serverless function will have access to the API key

04:08:57.780 --> 04:08:59.780
from a secure store.

04:08:59.780 --> 04:09:02.420
The serverless function will then make the call

04:09:02.420 --> 04:09:04.440
to the OpenAI API.

04:09:04.440 --> 04:09:06.520
The API will pass the response back

04:09:06.520 --> 04:09:07.940
to the serverless function,

04:09:07.940 --> 04:09:10.460
and the serverless function will pass the response

04:09:10.460 --> 04:09:11.940
back to the front-end,

04:09:11.940 --> 04:09:15.000
and we will use the completion from that response.

04:09:15.000 --> 04:09:19.160
But most importantly, this API key in its special store

04:09:19.160 --> 04:09:21.600
is never visible to the front-end,

04:09:21.600 --> 04:09:24.880
so it won't be visible in the DevTools Network tab.

04:09:24.880 --> 04:09:26.540
Now, there are a few prerequisites

04:09:26.540 --> 04:09:28.100
that I'll just mention quickly.

04:09:28.100 --> 04:09:30.540
You are going to need a free Netlify account.

04:09:30.540 --> 04:09:32.140
That's really easy to get.

04:09:32.140 --> 04:09:33.260
I'm also going to assume

04:09:33.260 --> 04:09:35.460
you have a basic knowledge of GitHub,

04:09:35.460 --> 04:09:39.420
because we will be deploying to Netlify directly from GitHub.

04:09:39.420 --> 04:09:42.020
If you know how to publish a project to a GitHub repo,

04:09:42.020 --> 04:09:43.500
that is enough.

04:09:43.500 --> 04:09:45.340
We'll also be making fetch requests,

04:09:45.340 --> 04:09:47.220
and if you've followed this course so far,

04:09:47.220 --> 04:09:48.820
you won't have any problem with that.

04:09:48.820 --> 04:09:51.100
We won't really be doing anything more sophisticated

04:09:51.100 --> 04:09:52.460
than we've already done,

04:09:52.460 --> 04:09:56.060
and you'll also need VS Code or a similar editor.

04:09:56.060 --> 04:09:57.820
Okay, that's the overview.

04:09:57.820 --> 04:09:59.360
Let's put it into practice.

